msgid "Refreshing access tokens"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`OidcClientRequestReactiveFilter`, `OidcClientRequestFilter`, and `Tokens` "
"producers refresh the current expired access token if a refresh token is "
"available."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additionally, you can use the `quarkus.oidc-client.refresh-token-time-skew` "
"property for preemptive access token refresh to avoid sending nearly expired "
"access tokens that might cause HTTP 401 errors."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For example, if this property is set to `3S` and the access token will "
"expire in less than 3 seconds, the token is refreshed automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the OIDC client refreshes the token during the current request "
"when it detects that the token has expired, or is nearly expired if the xref:"
"#quarkus-oidc-client_quarkus-oidc-client-refresh-token-time-skew[refresh "
"token time skew] is configured.\n"
"Performance-critical applications might want to avoid waiting for a possible "
"token refresh during incoming requests and configure an asynchronous token "
"refresh instead."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check every minute whether the current access token is expired and must be "
"refreshed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the access token needs to be refreshed but no refresh token is available, "
"an attempt is made to acquire a new token with a configured grant, such as "
"`client_credentials`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some OpenID Connect providers do not return a refresh token in a "
"`client_credentials` grant response.\n"
"For example, starting with Keycloak 12, a refresh token is not returned by "
"default for `client_credentials`.\n"
"Providers might also restrict how many times a refresh token can be used."
msgstr ""

msgid "Revoking access tokens"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your OpenID Connect provider, such as Keycloak, supports a token "
"revocation endpoint, you can use `OidcClient#revokeAccessToken` to revoke "
"the current access token.\n"
"The revocation endpoint URL is discovered alongside the token request URI or "
"can be configured with `quarkus.oidc-client.revoke-path`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You might want to revoke the access token if a REST client call that uses "
"this token fails with an HTTP `401` status code, or if the token has been "
"used for a long time and you want to refresh it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can do this by requesting a token refresh with a refresh token.\n"
"However, if the refresh token is unavailable, you can revoke the current "
"access token first and then request a new access token."
msgstr ""

